{%- import "python/_types.jinja" as types -%}
{#-
  The contract of one table's data layer: create, read, update, delete, and a
  search that filters over several columns and orders by a named column and a
  direction.

  Rendered once per table, per FR-RND-002 and FR-EX-005:

      tpl -d <schema> render python/repository --table <name> > datalayer/<schema>/<name>_repository.py

  The contract is rendered separately from the implementation so that a caller
  can depend on it without depending on how it is served, and so that the
  difference between the two is visible in the example rather than implied.

  It is a `typing.Protocol` and not an abstract base class, because a Protocol
  is satisfied structurally: the implementation this example renders beside it
  names no base class at all, and `mypy` still proves the two agree. An
  implementation a reader writes against another driver therefore satisfies the
  same contract without importing it.
-#}
{%- if not table.primary_key -%}
{{- fail("python/repository.jinja cannot render " ~ database.name ~ "." ~ table.name ~ ": the table declares no primary key, so read, update and delete have no key to address a row by.") -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set model = types.type_name(table.name) -%}
{%- set module = types.ident(table.name) -%}
{%- set qualified = database.name ~ "." ~ table.name -%}
{%- set auto -%}
{%- for column in table.columns %}{% if column is auto_increment %}<auto>{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- endset -%}
